#
# Scored with the RNG HELD FIXED across FOVs, so these counts are a real FOV
# effect, not auto_unstuck's dice - which is what invalidated the v1
# fov_search_rank* set (rank01: 0/120 at fixed seed, 107/120 across seeds).
# Counts are CLEAN: only steps where BOTH humans are actively pursuing a
# real subtask and pick different ones. Divergence held under all
# 3 seeds.
#
# human model: plain SteakLimitVisionHumanModel (NOT sticky - the sticky
#   wrapper stalls the human ~20 steps in with 1-2 subtasks touched)
# teammate: work (full-vision GreedySteakHumanModel)
# kb_update_delay: 3  <- REQUIRED. At the project
#   default of 0 every FOV learns the same things and inference is
#   impossible; the filter must use this same value.
# FOV triple (deg): 90, 139, 169
#   (sampled spread in cos(fov/2), the quantity in_bound() actually tests)
#
# clean pairwise subtask disagreement, whole episode: 7
# clean pairwise subtask disagreement, latter half   : 7
# RNG noise floor (same FOV, different seed)         : 1.1
# distinct subtasks (worst rollout): 8   distinct tiles: 30   min len: 76
